  "namingIssues": null,
  "existingDescription": "A 24-variant button set covering three emphasis levels (Primary, Neutral, Subtle) across two sizes and four interaction states. Each variant holds an optional start icon, a text label and an optional end icon, all driven by component properties.\n\nPURPOSE: The standard action trigger in the system. Primary carries the brand fill for the main action, Neutral uses a tertiary grey surface with a visible border, and Subtle is the lowest-emphasis option for secondary or inline actions.\n\nBEHAVIOUR: State is a variant property with Default, Hover, Disabled and Focus. Hover swaps the background token (Background/Brand/Hover for Primary, Background/Neutral/Tertiary Hover for Neutral). Disabled switches background, border, icon and text to the Disabled token family. Focus adds the Stroke/Focus Ring border token on top of the resting appearance. In code these map to CSS pseudo-classes and the disabled attribute rather than separate components.\n\nCOMPOSITION: Each variant contains two instances of a shared icon \"container\" component, one before and one after the label, each wrapping a single Icon vector. Both icon slots are instance-swap properties backed by a 576-icon library, defaulting to X (end) and Star (start). AI code generators should look for an existing Icon or icon-wrapper component in the development codebase before building a new one.\n\nUSAGE: Use Primary for the single most important action in a view, Neutral for supporting actions beside it, and Subtle where a button must sit quietly inside dense content. Use Has Icon Start or Has Icon End to add meaning, not decoration. For navigation to another page, use a link rather than this component.\n\nCODE GENERATION NOTES: Build one button component with variant, size and icon props instead of 24 separate components. Label is a plain text property, so expose it as children. Keep both icon slots optional and hide the wrapper entirely when the matching boolean is false, so spacing tokens Space/300 and Space/200 do not leave a gap. Disabled must set aria-disabled or the disabled attribute, not just the visual tokens. Focus styling should come from :focus-visible so it only appears for keyboard users. The set uses Icon/Danger/Tertiary in at least one place, so check whether a danger treatment is intended before mapping icon colours blindly.",
